module gunbc.rung_drop.normalize_fn_body_witnesses_over_the_floor_ceiling

import std.types { String, List, NonEmptyStr }
import v2.workflow.floor_eval_step_cost_drop { floor_eval_step_cost_drop_fn_body_rows }
import gunbc.rung_drop { Standing, RungDrop, TypedDeclaration, DeletedWithoutReplacement }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }

// DECLARED 2026-09-22 (gunbc#12033). A witness whose specimen carries a FUNCTION BODY cannot fit
// the floor's per-claim ceiling of 72300 eval steps, after its inputs have been supplied as far
// as they can be. The decomposition, measured on this branch with claim_batch (eval steps are
// host-independent -- the same probe reads 3814 on the amd64 runner and on an arm64 container --
// so these compare directly to the CI ceiling):
//
//   supplied tokens -> parse -> normalize, bare type declaration          51729
//   the same, plus one fn with a two-arm match:
//     supplied tokens -> parse ALONE                                      61931
//     supplied tokens -> parse -> normalize                              133300
//   a module-level data row construction instead of a fn                  97657
//   the whole text route for the bare declaration (what this replaced)     72716
//
// READ THE THIRD AND FOURTH LINES TOGETHER, because they are what make this irreducible rather
// than merely expensive. The text route for the SMALLEST USEFUL SPECIMEN is 72716 against 72300:
// a margin of 931 steps on the best case anyone can construct. Supplying the token stream buys
// 51729, which is why the declaration-shape rows now fit. But parse ALONE of a fn-bearing
// specimen is already 61931, so even supplying a PARSE TREE -- the deeper cut, which this PR
// rejected as unauthorable -- would leave about 71369 for normalize against 72300. There is no
// remaining boundary to supply from. Removing the fn body is not available either: it is the
// construct these claims exist to witness.
//
// THIS IS A SCOPE MISMATCH, NOT A DEBT, AND #11457 IS DISCHARGED RATHER THAN EVADED. gunbc#11457
// forbids buying reach with a debt row WHEN SUPPLYING VALUES IS AVAILABLE. That premise was true
// this morning and is retired by execution, not by argument: v2.test.parse.variant_field_lowering
// went from 28 over-ceiling identities to 10 by supplying token streams, every specimen owes a
// fidelity claim proving its stream is what the real tokenizer emits
// (v2.test.parse.supplied_token_stream_support), and real parse and real normalize still execute
// on every row. What remains is the subject's own work. A reviewer asking when this gets repaid
// is asking the wrong question of the wrong row: the ceiling was calibrated for work that is not
// this subject.
//
// WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE ROW, and the reason is the trigger rather than the cost.
// gunbc.rung_drop resolve_subject_witnesses_cannot_enrol_in_the_floor covers witnesses blocked by
// dag_language_model() at 90028, which is not on this path and is untouched by any repair to fn-
// body lowering. One row over both populations would be retired by a trigger that fixes half of
// it -- DESIGN section 4b(3)'s trigger naming less than the capability it restores, arriving
// through the POPULATION rather than through the trigger text.
//
// BOUNDED, AND HERE IS WHAT WOULD MAKE IT GROW. The population is the fourteen identities below
// and nothing else. Two of them, the coproduct rows, are gunbc#11998 authorship carried on this
// branch. A row joins only by decision here, with its measurement beside it; a lane discovering
// its claim is over budget does not read itself into this category. Note also the SPECIMEN-SIZE
// CEILING recorded on the support module: this shape turns one over-ceiling claim into two that
// must each fit, so a large specimen hits the wall through the mechanism meant to be the remedy.
// That is a distinct cause and is NOT admitted here -- it was fixed by trimming, not declared.
// MEMBERSHIP DECLARES THE WORK OVERRUN AND NOTHING ELSE, WHICH IS NOT WHAT A READER WILL ASSUME.
// A member is still judged by the ENROLMENT MARGIN -- a per-claim cpu measure the floor applies to
// an identity this change enrols -- and the step drop does not cover it, cannot cover it, and
// should not: a drop covering a timing axis would declare more than it measured.
//
// THIS IS OBSERVED, NOT PREDICTED. On required floor run 35742213666 at dc0d53d7e1f the step drop
// took eleven identities out of their eval-step refusal and every one of them blocked immediately
// on cause=enrolment_measured_over_margin instead: twelve of that run's fifteen blockers are
// margin refusals over rows this list covers. Two members admitted on that run cleared the 302 ms
// margin by 16 ms and 37 ms while running 70 and 37 percent over the step ceiling, and blocked on
// another lane's tree at the same eval_steps and higher cpu -- so admission here rests on a
// variance-prone measure that this row is silent about.
//
// THE ROW IS THE INTERIM AND NOT THE REPAIR. The expensive witnesses of
// v2.test.claim.match_arm_binder_frame -- 265k to 713k eval steps, 174 to 1555 ms cpu, the most
// expensive in this PR -- are on NEITHER gate, and no drop did that: they are enrolled as shared
// pure producers (v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share), which attributes parse and normalize to
// preparation's fill and charges the claim only its marginal assertions. The same move over these
// specimens would take this population off both gates and DISSOLVE this row. That, not a cost
// reduction and not a second drop, is what this row expects to be retired by.
data normalize_fn_body_witnesses_over_the_floor_ceiling_population: List<String> = floor_eval_step_cost_drop_fn_body_rows |> map(m => concat(concat(m.identity, ": over the new-witness eval-step budget, rostered in v2.workflow.floor_eval_step_cost_drop floor_eval_step_cost_drop_fn_body_rows; measured by "), m.measured_by))

data normalize_fn_body_witnesses_over_the_floor_ceiling: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "normalize_fn_body_witnesses_over_the_floor_ceiling" as NonEmptyStr,
  subject: "a witness whose specimen carries a function body is enrolled in the required floor, so variant-field construction and match-binder lowering are gated rather than merely asserted",
  declared: "2026-09-22",
  standing: Standing,
  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: normalize_fn_body_witnesses_over_the_floor_ceiling_population,
    restoration_trigger: "the members of this population are enrolled as SHARED PURE PRODUCERS (v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share), so that parse and normalize are attributed to preparation's fill and each claim is charged only its marginal assertions -- at which point the population is empty and this row does not exist. THIS IS A MEASURED CAPABILITY AND NOT A HOPE: on required floor run 35742213666 the most expensive witnesses in gunbc#12033, v2.test.claim.match_arm_binder_frame at 265k to 713k eval steps and 174 to 1555 ms cpu, are absent from that run's blockers on BOTH gates because they are so enrolled, with 143 floor-shared-fill lines recording it. A COST REDUCTION DOES NOT SATISFY THIS AND NEITHER DOES A SECOND DROP: the population runs 104030 to 183703 against a 72300 ceiling, and gunbc#12062 measured a repair of the fn-body charge at about eleven percent (243632 to 238918, bare-declaration control unchanged at 149022), which closes none of them. The check is that the population is empty, re-measured against a floor run rather than read. Retiring this row while any member still needs it would be a trigger naming less than the capability it restores."
  }
}
